{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0cd8b1768ab0a987e875f6177d8da2afd804a072e43b1f82e6093d28436edc8f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README invites pull requests, welcoming ideas, issues, and improvements from contributors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f797c30b3207becbc9f9202930e7bc619e50887fd7cbbc8cfa83b842400fca6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool provides colored terminal output for readability and can copy suggested commands to the clipboard."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2d2b6e94cc669471028786e6a9b9b87fc3d8d71a71ca04da798f7c6c91c5b8ab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Using the Ollama feature requires Ollama to be installed and running locally (e.g. on localhost:11434); local models like phi-4-mini are also supported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_389960a00fbcaa45c19256f1b51d05756440f3486066e346606d8126250e1f9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ollama-backed models are selected via flags such as --ollama --model llama3, as shown in documented example invocations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c8597706cef7550f3c17ccbaa10c7073897474bce29a2b7a92682866ca07846"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is designed to run fully locally with no OpenAI API key, sending no data to the cloud; models run locally."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4499c0933821ec968476d473cd6d5ebda00766c945fa6c9cc114b684d43154a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The workflow sends the prompt to the Ollama API, returns a shell command suggestion, then prompts the user to execute, copy, or abort."},{"claim_ids":["clm_50e947a35618105cc778aa6581da8f51a1f1bc3eaebf619752095cc0900c7da8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed (copyright 2025 codingmo) and positions itself as a fully open-source CLI AI assistant inspired by OpenAI Codex."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8287ecb9283d7f6d7134077d0b58886f4f1cf8c0b43f97d1c094961eea04cde0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a CLI named open-codex that accepts a natural-language prompt and returns a suggested shell command, e.g. open-codex \"list all folders\"."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9419446b1e1cb3da63eb324ec1590b4461a49df55b9ca683484e448e7a517996"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README lists interactive context-aware mode, full chat mode, function calling, voice input, command history/undo, and a plugin system as future plans, implying they are not yet available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b13caeab24680b6bd9783e13f95477478ca9bf580c463df8324ce76855d3a427"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the README, suggested commands are executed only after the user's explicit confirmation, with options to copy to clipboard or abort instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e958592e5a6c015519ce6be7d000cdb473c108f96fb77c6360dc429d8cff38bc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation options include Homebrew (recommended for macOS), pipx for cross-platform install, or cloning and running pip install."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0cd8b1768ab0a987e875f6177d8da2afd804a072e43b1f82e6093d28436edc8f","clm_0f797c30b3207becbc9f9202930e7bc619e50887fd7cbbc8cfa83b842400fca6","clm_2d2b6e94cc669471028786e6a9b9b87fc3d8d71a71ca04da798f7c6c91c5b8ab","clm_389960a00fbcaa45c19256f1b51d05756440f3486066e346606d8126250e1f9f","clm_3c8597706cef7550f3c17ccbaa10c7073897474bce29a2b7a92682866ca07846","clm_4499c0933821ec968476d473cd6d5ebda00766c945fa6c9cc114b684d43154a3","clm_50e947a35618105cc778aa6581da8f51a1f1bc3eaebf619752095cc0900c7da8","clm_8287ecb9283d7f6d7134077d0b58886f4f1cf8c0b43f97d1c094961eea04cde0","clm_9419446b1e1cb3da63eb324ec1590b4461a49df55b9ca683484e448e7a517996","clm_b13caeab24680b6bd9783e13f95477478ca9bf580c463df8324ce76855d3a427","clm_e958592e5a6c015519ce6be7d000cdb473c108f96fb77c6360dc429d8cff38bc"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_7f67dd96f7c7416884e25a8a521a944a","id":"pg_8207567773795bac816ca8c6f089f937","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/codingmoh-open-codex-readme-md-87aaaed1cea9-a8c6f089f937.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_